  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 133 AM CST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nMostly sunny skies and light westerly winds to prevail over the\nregion today. Meanwhile early morning satellite water vapor \nimagery shows a healthy PV wave over northern Nevada moving \neastward. This system will eject from the Rockies late tonight \nwith modest lift generating rain showers over southwest Kansas. \nThis system will continue to move east across Kansas with rain \nshowers spreading over south central and southeast Kansas during\nthe day on Thursday. Dry weather to follow for Friday as \nbriefing upper level ridging influences the region. \n\nGFS model/GEFS ensembles show a weather system deepening and \nejecting southeast from the Rockies across western Kansas into \nOklahoma for the weekend. Moisture will be lacking and remain well \nsouth of the region, therefore the system should move across the \ncentral plains with little to no precipitation. The dry weather \npattern looks to continue into next week with a gradual warming \ntrend expected as upper level ridging re-establishes itself over \nKansas.",
